Hey, Dawson, where you goin'?

152
00:13:11,631 --> 00:13:14,100
Right, a big thanks
to the entire squad

153
00:13:14,133 --> 00:13:16,469
For all your hard work.

154
00:13:16,503 --> 00:13:18,971
Now, you all have
a valid place,

155
00:13:19,005 --> 00:13:20,940
But this is
the Grand Final.

156
00:13:20,973 --> 00:13:23,676
It's our first in seven years.

157
00:13:23,710 --> 00:13:25,378
- Whoo!
- Yeah!

158
00:13:26,913 --> 00:13:28,548
Come on, boys.

159
00:13:30,517 --> 00:13:32,151
I believe
that we've picked a team

160
00:13:32,184 --> 00:13:34,554
That can really do the job.

161
00:13:34,587 --> 00:13:35,888
Yeah!

162
00:13:37,557 --> 00:13:40,860
Backs: Ranking,

163
00:13:40,893 --> 00:13:44,697
Egan, Kirwan,

164
00:13:44,731 --> 00:13:50,537
Knights, Irish and Gale.

165
00:13:50,570 --> 00:13:51,771
Forwards:

166
00:13:51,804 --> 00:13:54,641
Milkey, Franky...

167
00:13:56,576 --> 00:13:59,646
Young, Morts...

168
00:13:59,679 --> 00:14:01,448
I'll take it.
I'll take it.

169
00:14:01,481 --> 00:14:03,950
Big Gerry Walsh and Touty.

170
00:14:06,453 --> 00:14:08,555
Followers:

171
00:14:08,588 --> 00:14:10,957
Robbo,

172
00:14:10,990 --> 00:14:12,892
Nicky Reagan,

173
00:14:12,925 --> 00:14:15,061
Costa.

174
00:14:15,094 --> 00:14:18,498
Interchange: Tully...

175
00:14:20,032 --> 00:14:22,969
Bennett, Gillespie,

176
00:14:26,038 --> 00:14:27,674
Dawson.

177
00:14:28,608 --> 00:14:32,144
Right.
The team meeting's at noon.

178
00:14:32,178 --> 00:14:34,113
Now you all know
what's at stake.

179
00:14:40,787 --> 00:14:44,090
Come and talk to me
or to Joe...

180
00:14:44,123 --> 00:14:46,526
If the game plan's
not crystal.

181
00:14:48,094 --> 00:14:49,696
That's it.

182
00:15:03,810 --> 00:15:06,613
♪ Two hearts burning
on a hillside ♪

183
00:15:06,646 --> 00:15:09,048
♪ Turning round
the blazing sun ♪

184
00:15:11,117 --> 00:15:14,487
♪ Fever burning
in her head that's turning ♪

185
00:15:14,521 --> 00:15:16,689
♪ Round the things she's done

186
00:15:18,625 --> 00:15:21,694
♪ Free your heart
That is the hardest part ♪

187
00:15:21,728 --> 00:15:24,831
♪ He says
your heart won't lie ♪

188
00:15:38,711 --> 00:15:40,647
Tommy! Tommy!

189
00:15:47,887 --> 00:15:50,089
- Morts, where you going?
- Tommy!

190
00:15:51,791 --> 00:15:55,094
♪ Heed that feeling
in your bones ♪

191
00:15:55,127 --> 00:15:58,565
♪ For your heart knows
you'll never win ♪

192
00:15:58,598 --> 00:16:01,100
♪ Till you're free from him

193
00:16:02,835 --> 00:16:04,070
Hey! Hey!

194
00:16:05,772 --> 00:16:07,106
- Come on, Tommy!
- They stole our balls!

195
00:16:07,139 --> 00:16:08,107
Come here, you little shits!

196
00:16:10,176 --> 00:16:13,580
♪ Don't look back
There is no use in wonderin' ♪

197
00:16:13,613 --> 00:16:15,548
♪ Just how or why

198
00:16:17,584 --> 00:16:20,319
♪ If you leave now,
you might just make it home ♪

199
00:16:20,352 --> 00:16:23,089
♪ Before the morning light

200
00:16:24,791 --> 00:16:26,559
♪ Tired and poor

201
00:16:26,593 --> 00:16:30,797
♪ You kneel at history's door
tonight ♪

202
00:16:55,955 --> 00:16:58,691
Oh, my soul!

203
00:16:58,725 --> 00:16:59,692
Surprise.

204
00:16:59,726 --> 00:17:01,661
Tommy!

205
00:17:01,694 --> 00:17:04,030
So how you holding up?

206
00:17:04,063 --> 00:17:06,699
We hadn't spoken in years.

207
00:17:08,901 --> 00:17:10,569
It's okay, Mum.

208
00:17:13,305 --> 00:17:16,743
You know, he was crushed
about what happened.

209
00:17:17,910 --> 00:17:19,345
With you boys.

210
00:17:20,747 --> 00:17:23,049
Yeah.

211
00:17:23,082 --> 00:17:25,885
Will you catch up
with any of them?

212
00:17:25,918 --> 00:17:28,087
- Yeah, I want to.
- Mm-hmm.

213
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:31,791
I think I might, uh,
might see Rose.

214
00:17:31,824 --> 00:17:35,027
Well!

215
00:17:35,061 --> 00:17:37,964
That's...
That's good, my love.

216
00:17:51,744 --> 00:17:58,718
♪ Those thieving birds

217
00:18:00,887 --> 00:18:07,326
♪ Hang strung
from an empty nest ♪

218
00:18:07,359 --> 00:18:14,133
♪ This swan-plagued pond

219
00:18:16,402 --> 00:18:23,109
♪ Forsaken and underwhelmed

220
00:18:23,142 --> 00:18:30,149
♪ Those leaving words

221
00:18:32,351 --> 00:18:39,859
♪ Hang strong
from an emptiness ♪

222
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:54,774
♪ Hang strung
from an empty nest ♪

223
00:18:54,807 --> 00:18:57,944
♪ Those thieving birds

224
00:18:57,977 --> 00:18:59,979
All right, listen up!

225
00:19:00,012 --> 00:19:01,881
It's gonna come down to will.

226
00:19:01,914 --> 00:19:05,885
The will to win
and how hard you want it.

227
00:19:05,918 --> 00:19:09,989
Gonna hit their boys hard
and hit those packs even harder.

228
00:19:11,223 --> 00:19:12,959
Have you got it in you?

229
00:19:12,992 --> 00:19:14,293
Yes!

230
00:19:14,326 --> 00:19:17,329
- How tough are we gonna be?
- Cowboy tough!

231
00:19:17,363 --> 00:19:19,966
Let's get it now!

232
00:19:36,182 --> 00:19:39,451
Go, Tigers!

233
00:19:46,993 --> 00:19:48,961
Good afternoon and welcome
to the Torquay Oval

234
00:19:48,995 --> 00:19:51,397
For the all-important
Grand Final clash.

235
00:19:51,430 --> 00:19:53,933
The respective sides
taking up their positions.

236
00:19:53,966 --> 00:19:57,203
You can almost just sense
the atmosphere is palpable.

237
00:19:57,236 --> 00:19:58,370
It is electric.

238
00:19:58,404 --> 00:19:59,405
The ferals on that
other side of the ground

239
00:19:59,438 --> 00:20:02,875
And the more demure
and more mature

240
00:20:02,909 --> 00:20:04,143
Torquay Tiger audience,

241
00:20:04,176 --> 00:20:06,378
Who really don't know
what is in store for them.

242
00:20:20,059 --> 00:20:22,829
And here we go.
Ball's in the air.

243
00:20:22,862 --> 00:20:26,365
Anglesea with the tap, but
straight down to Nicky Reagan.

244
00:20:26,398 --> 00:20:28,968
- Reagan boots it long.
- Way down! Way down!

245
00:20:29,001 --> 00:20:30,937
And look,
there's Mortimer on a lead.

246
00:20:30,970 --> 00:20:33,005
He takes a very strong mark.

247
00:20:33,039 --> 00:20:37,043
Strong grab, directly in front
from 35 to 40 meters out.

248
00:20:37,076 --> 00:20:40,913
Hits truly. And the first point
to the Tigers!

249
00:20:40,947 --> 00:20:43,215
Perhaps the only
surprise selection today

250
00:20:43,249 --> 00:20:45,251
Is the omission of Tommy Dunn.

251
00:20:45,284 --> 00:20:47,419
Dunn had played
every game this year,

252
00:20:47,453 --> 00:20:50,056
But Coach Chang in his wisdom
had left him out.

253
00:20:50,089 --> 00:20:54,160
We'll see what consequences
that has on the game.

254
00:20:54,193 --> 00:20:55,494
Dawson, with great dexterity,

255
00:20:55,527 --> 00:20:57,496
Breaks one tackle,
runs down the wing.

256
00:20:57,529 --> 00:21:00,332
Ford up, great tackle.
Didn't feel the hit coming.

257
00:21:00,366 --> 00:21:03,469
Should have got rid of it.
He's holding the ball.

258
00:21:03,502 --> 00:21:05,271
Come on, come on,
get in, get in!

259
00:21:05,304 --> 00:21:07,539
Robbo with the tap, but it's
straight down to Harkins.

260
00:21:07,573 --> 00:21:10,409
He dispatches one opponent,
kicks long.

261
00:21:10,442 --> 00:21:13,545
Dial goes up.
What a screener for Anglesea!

262
00:21:13,579 --> 00:21:16,148
He juggled it beautifully
as he came down.

263
00:21:19,385 --> 00:21:21,453
Dial slots the goal from 30.

264
00:21:24,123 --> 00:21:25,958
