00:39:14,395 --> 00:39:15,329
He wanted it so bad, mate.

527
00:39:15,363 --> 00:39:18,999
It was our first Grand Final
since you left.

528
00:39:24,372 --> 00:39:27,608
So you gonna come for a roll?

529
00:39:27,641 --> 00:39:29,343
You're lookin' at
the new bronze-medal,

530
00:39:29,377 --> 00:39:31,011
Fourth-division champion.

531
00:39:34,548 --> 00:39:37,485
So if you only got bronze,
how are you the champion?

532
00:39:40,521 --> 00:39:41,622
Count back.

533
00:39:42,723 --> 00:39:44,325
Look at that concentration.

534
00:39:45,693 --> 00:39:47,761
Nice, Franky.

535
00:39:47,795 --> 00:39:49,163
It's good
to have you back, fella,

536
00:39:49,197 --> 00:39:50,431
Despite the circumstances,
you know?

537
00:39:50,464 --> 00:39:54,302
Yeah, mate. I'm sorry I've been
so hopeless staying in touch.

538
00:39:54,335 --> 00:39:56,270
Ah, you're all right.
You're all right.

539
00:39:56,304 --> 00:39:58,572
Tommy? Tommy.

540
00:39:58,606 --> 00:40:00,174
- Hey.
- Tommy!

541
00:40:00,208 --> 00:40:01,542
- How are ya?
- Good, man.

542
00:40:01,575 --> 00:40:03,744
- Good to see ya.
- Good to see you.

543
00:40:03,777 --> 00:40:06,147
- Hey, money bags.
- Dude.

544
00:40:06,180 --> 00:40:09,150
This guy's a property
developer now. Ka-ching.

545
00:40:09,183 --> 00:40:11,319
Land down here,
who would've thought it?

546
00:40:11,352 --> 00:40:14,688
Just lucky, mate. Some guys
at the Cats were putting in.

547
00:40:14,722 --> 00:40:16,590
Right place, right time.

548
00:40:16,624 --> 00:40:19,093
Play five games,
hit the jackpot.

549
00:40:21,795 --> 00:40:24,098
Remember when Chang caught us
having bongs in juniors?

550
00:40:24,132 --> 00:40:25,166
Yeah, he smacked me.

551
00:40:25,199 --> 00:40:26,800
So scared of him back then.

552
00:40:26,834 --> 00:40:29,403
- He can't do that anymore.
- Bongs?

553
00:40:29,437 --> 00:40:32,106
- Hitting kids.
- Didn't do it again, though.

554
00:40:32,140 --> 00:40:33,407
- Bongs?
- Yes!

555
00:40:35,809 --> 00:40:38,579
- Good one, Tommy.
- Oh!

556
00:40:40,514 --> 00:40:44,252
Ah, one down, Tommy.

557
00:40:44,285 --> 00:40:46,387
Franky's holding shot.

558
00:40:47,688 --> 00:40:54,462
♪♪

559
00:40:56,497 --> 00:41:01,702
♪♪

560
00:41:07,541 --> 00:41:10,878
All right.
Who wants another?

561
00:41:10,911 --> 00:41:12,846
Shouldn't have asked,
should I?

562
00:41:14,582 --> 00:41:16,684
Glad he's driving.

563
00:41:20,921 --> 00:41:23,824
Ah. Yeah, Chang once told me

564
00:41:23,857 --> 00:41:26,894
That he'd never seen
a better kicker inside 30.

565
00:41:26,927 --> 00:41:28,862
Said I could've played AFL.

566
00:41:30,198 --> 00:41:32,400
In a different era.

567
00:41:32,433 --> 00:41:33,601
Hmm.

568
00:41:35,636 --> 00:41:38,472
It's tough to get noticed
out here on the coast.

569
00:41:40,408 --> 00:41:42,810
Everyone's good inside 30,
Franky, you dipstick.

570
00:41:42,843 --> 00:41:46,414
Jackie? He still nails 'em
from 30, and he's 82.

571
00:41:48,582 --> 00:41:50,484
Well, I've seen him miss.

572
00:41:54,755 --> 00:41:58,359
And Chang, he was real good to
me when I got delisted.

573
00:41:58,392 --> 00:42:00,661
Came and saw me
in the hospital heaps, too.

574
00:42:00,694 --> 00:42:02,830
Yeah, he was proud of you.

575
00:42:02,863 --> 00:42:06,634
Yeah, real champion.
Doped up on antidepressants.

576
00:42:06,667 --> 00:42:09,203
Mate, you played five more games

577
00:42:09,237 --> 00:42:10,538
Than the rest of us
put together.

578
00:42:10,571 --> 00:42:15,309
You know, you did it. You did
it. You played AFL.

579
00:42:15,343 --> 00:42:16,344
Yeah.

580
00:42:16,377 --> 00:42:17,678
Dude!

581
00:42:17,711 --> 00:42:19,647
I'll bring him over.

582
00:42:25,753 --> 00:42:27,421
I'll catch you later.

583
00:42:35,996 --> 00:42:38,499
Tom. Tom, wait up.

584
00:42:45,739 --> 00:42:47,675
Tom, we gotta let it go.

585
00:42:48,876 --> 00:42:51,011
Really?

586
00:42:51,044 --> 00:42:54,014
Instead of just... Instead of
fighting to clear your name,

587
00:42:54,047 --> 00:42:57,017
You just walked out
looking guilty.

588
00:42:57,050 --> 00:42:59,853
Is that right, is it?

589
00:42:59,887 --> 00:43:02,356
I'm sorry it happened.

590
00:43:02,390 --> 00:43:05,793
Are you sorry,
or are you sorry it happened?

591
00:43:05,826 --> 00:43:07,961
You know, Sammy's age might have
had everyone in a stir,

592
00:43:07,995 --> 00:43:09,897
But she wasn't a baby.

593
00:43:11,499 --> 00:43:12,933
I lost 13 years

594
00:43:12,966 --> 00:43:16,370
Because of some stupid photos
in the newspaper.

595
00:43:16,404 --> 00:43:17,771
Yeah, don't forget the draft.

596
00:43:17,805 --> 00:43:19,640
The Cats would've come around.

597
00:43:19,673 --> 00:43:22,510
Yeah, okay, they got cold feet.
But face it, you gave up.

598
00:43:22,543 --> 00:43:24,612
If that helps you
sleep at night, mate,

599
00:43:24,645 --> 00:43:26,847
I never gave up.

600
00:43:26,880 --> 00:43:30,451
You forget that I lost
everything that night too.

601
00:43:30,484 --> 00:43:32,353
I don't forget, okay?

602
00:43:32,386 --> 00:43:34,522
I think about what you did
all the time.

603
00:43:51,004 --> 00:43:52,906
Thank you, everybody,
for coming today...

604
00:43:52,940 --> 00:43:55,409
To celebrate
an amazing life.

605
00:43:59,012 --> 00:44:00,681
Thanks for coming,
everybody.

606
00:44:10,090 --> 00:44:12,460
So you think you might
stay for a while?

607
00:44:14,795 --> 00:44:16,330
I don't know, Mum.

608
00:44:23,070 --> 00:44:24,738
- Mrs. Dunn...
- Nick!

609
00:44:24,772 --> 00:44:27,608
You planning on stepping up
from assistant coach

610
00:44:27,641 --> 00:44:30,744
To lead the boys
in the Grand Final?

611
00:44:30,778 --> 00:44:33,046
I didn't know you're
assistant coach.

612
00:44:33,080 --> 00:44:34,114
Tommy Dunn!

613
00:44:34,147 --> 00:44:35,849
Right now we're just here
to pay our respects.

614
00:44:35,883 --> 00:44:37,818
Tommy, do you want to say
a few words about Chang?

615
00:44:37,851 --> 00:44:40,354
- No, thanks.
- We haven't heard from you...

616
00:44:40,388 --> 00:44:41,722
Sorry, guys.
This is the wrong place!

617
00:44:42,956 --> 00:44:44,592
Okay. Take it easy.

618
00:44:48,529 --> 00:44:50,364
Barwon Heads, what a setting.

619
00:44:50,398 --> 00:44:51,799
The Tigers versus the Seagulls.

620
00:44:51,832 --> 00:44:53,701
First game back for the Tigers

621
00:44:53,734 --> 00:44:57,070
Since their big Grand Final
victory in 2002.

622
00:44:57,104 --> 00:44:59,673
Looking back at the Tigers'
bench, there's Wilson, Knights,

623
00:44:59,707 --> 00:45:01,509
And Tommy Dunn,
selected for round one

624
00:45:01,542 --> 00:45:03,777
After his omission
from the Grand Final.

625
00:45:07,147 --> 00:45:08,382
The ball's up.

626
00:45:08,416 --> 00:45:10,784
Nicky Reagan at ground level
slickly picks it up,

627
00:45:10,818 --> 00:45:13,521
Dodges one, dodges two,
onto his right foot.

628
00:45:13,554 --> 00:45:16,424
A long kick into
the forward line. Mortimer!

629
00:45:16,457 --> 00:45:19,660
Did you see that? They've really
gotta run it through Morts more.

630
00:45:19,693 --> 00:45:21,795
Morts?
Morts, Morts, Morts!

631
00:45:21,829 --> 00:45:23,431
Getting a little obsessive,
Sammy?

632
00:45:24,932 --> 00:45:26,834
Mortimer again,
this time at ground level.

633
00:45:26,867 --> 00:45:27,901
Picks it up, steps.

634
00:45:27,935 --> 00:45:30,037
It's good! A goal!

635
00:45:30,070 --> 00:45:32,105
He's ripping this game apart.

636
00:45:34,041 --> 00:45:36,009
Let's give it to 'em, boys!

637
00:45:36,043 --> 00:45:37,945
A strong lead. It's Dunston
with outstretched hands.

638
00:45:37,978 --> 00:45:39,413
Takes a strong mark.

639
00:45:39,447 --> 00:45:41,048
35 meters out,
directly in front.

640
00:45:41,081 --> 00:45:43,451
The conversion
is absolutely perfect.

641
00:45:43,484 --> 00:45:46,086
Barwon Heads
right back in the game.

642
00:45:46,119 --> 00:45:47,888
Nicky Reagan
to Jack Didier.

643
00:45:47,921 --> 00:45:49,823
He kicks long.

644
00:45:49,857 --> 00:45:52,493
Franky caught behind.
He's not chasing.

645
00:45:52,526 --> 00:45:53,827
What the hell was that?

646
00:45:53,861 --> 00:45:55,963
He really doesn't look like
he's got his heart in it today.

647
00:45:55,996 --> 00:45:57,965
He's gotta give chase
or he's off!

648
00:45:57,998 --> 00:46:01,168
As expected, he incurred
the total wrath of Coach Chang.

649
00:46:01,201 --> 00:46:03,471
Clearly not a happy chappy.

650
00:46:03,504 --> 00:46:04,805
Franky, if you're not
gonna chase him,

651
00:46:04,838 --> 00:46:06,206
Get off the
bloody green.

652
00:46:06,239 --> 00:46:08,842
- I don't need to kick goals?
- Just chase, mate.

653
00:46:11,579 --> 00:46:13,947
Try runnin' off
with one nut, mate.

654
00:46:13,981 --> 00:46:16,484
Reagan up to Irish.

655
00:46:16,517 --> 00:46:19,887
Irish kicks long, finds Tanner.
Tanner out in front this time!

656
00:46:19,920 --> 00:46:22,222
Takes a good mark.
He bananas a goal.

657
00:46:22,255 --> 00:46:25,559
It's looking good!
It's through the big uprights.

658
00:46:25,593 --> 00:46:27,828
He looks to Chang
on the bench as if to say,

659
00:46:27,861 --> 00:46:30,564
"Stick that up your jumper!"

660
00:46:30,598 --> 00:46:32,666
Reagan handballs
over to Franky Tanner.

661
00:46:32,700 --> 00:46:34,502
On his right foot, steps,
a goal!

662
00:46:34,535 --> 00:46:36,504
Oh, in just a few minutes

663
00:46:36,537 --> 00:46:39,106
The big man has brought
his presence into the game.

664
00:46:39,139 --> 00:46:41,609
Talk about swift redemption.

665
00:46:41,642 --> 00:46:43,210
And doesn't he love it!

666
00:46:43,243 --> 00:46:46,680
And don't the Barwon Heads fans
just hate him!

667
00:46:46,714 --> 00:46:50,150
Dawson dodges one.
Oh, he's gonna get run down.

668
00:46:50,183 --> 00:46:52,219
Hogue is gonna get him
from behind!

669
00:46:52,252 --> 00:46:56,123
Hogue with a big tackle.
Selfish play from Dawson.

670
00:46:56,156 --> 00:46:57,057
Pull him off.

671
00:46:57,090 --> 00:46:59,192
Looks like Dawson's
getting dragged.

672
00:46:59,226 --> 00:47:02,496
No room in Chang's manual
for that lazy selfish pride.

673
00:47:02,530 --> 00:47:05,232
Could Tommy Dunn
get his first opportunity?

674
00:47:05,265 --> 00:47:09,002
Yep. Up steps Tommy Dunn.

675
00:47:09,036 --> 00:47:13,507
His first game since his
omission in the Grand Final.

676
00:47:13,541 --> 00:47:15,543
Dunn's straight back
into the thick of it.

677
00:47:15,576 --> 00:47:16,877
Strong tackle.

678
00:47:16,910 --> 00:47:19,012
Dunn again.
Another strong tackle.

679
00:47:19,046 --> 00:47:22,049
Earns the free kick.
That's all on the ball.

680
00:47:22,082 --> 00:47:23,984
The one-percenters
from Tommy Dunn today

681
00:47:24,017 --> 00:47:25,085
Have been huge.

682
00:47:25,986 --> 00:47:27,254
Reagan on a long run.

683
00:47:27,287 --> 00:47:30,257
Dodges one or two,
takes a bounce.

684
00:47:30,290 --> 00:47:33,794
Off the ball, Tommy Dunn!
A huge shirtfront!

685
00:47:33,827 --> 00:47:36,764
And now a long kick to
the forward line. Mortimer!

686
00:47:36,797 --> 00:47:38,165
A huge grab!

687
00:47:40,167 --> 00:47:42,636
Tommy Dunn at the pegs
snaps a goal!

688
00:47:42,670 --> 00:47:45,072
Welcome back, Tommy Dunn!

689
00:47:45,105 --> 00:47:47,941
Dunn running back
with the flight of the ball.

690
00:47:47,975 --> 00:47:50,778
Oh, what a courageous mark
from Tommy Dunn.

691
00:47:50,811 --> 00:47:51,912
Backing into a pack,

692
00:47:51,945 --> 00:47:54,548
The toughest thing
you can do in football.

693
00:47:54,582 --> 00:47:56,850
But I think he's injured
himself fairly badly.

694
00:47:56,884 --> 00:47:59,052
It could be his ribs.

695
00:47:59,086 --> 00:48:01,221
Good courage, Tommy!

696
00:48:01,254 --> 00:48:03,290
The runners
are heading out to him.

697
00:48:03,323 --> 00:48:05,993
I think they're calling
for a stretcher.

698
00:48:10,063 --> 00:48:12,265
Hey. You okay?

699
00:48:12,299 --> 00:48:15,202
Please don't tell
the boys I spewed.

700
00:48:15,235 --> 00:48:16,937
So I'm weaving left,
I'm weaving right.

701
00:48:16,970 --> 00:48:19,673
Our mate kicks it long,
but Tanner's leaping...

702
00:48:19,707 --> 00:48:22,309
Ohh!

703
00:48:22,342 --> 00:48:24,011
And he took a screamer,

704
00:48:24,044 --> 00:48:26,647
Which ultimately tubed
the game for everybody.

705
00:48:26,680 --> 00:48:28,248
Well, if you were out there.

706
00:48:28,281 --> 00:48:30,017
- We won, didn't we?
- My hero.

707
00:48:32,285 --> 00:48:33,787
I only played for 10 minutes.

708
00:48:33,820 --> 00:48:35,655
What no, hang on, Tommy.

709
00:48:35,689 --> 00:48:37,924
There was a fair bit
of Cowboy tough.

710
00:48:37,957 --> 00:48:39,258
You won us the match.

711
00:48:39,292 --> 00:48:41,561
Well, debatable.

712
00:48:41,595 --> 00:48:43,229
Here.

713
00:48:44,230 --> 00:48:45,899
Who kicked the winning goal?

714
00:48:45,932 --> 00:48:47,266
Nicky Reagan.

715
00:48:47,300 --> 00:48:49,002
Who gave it to Nicky Reagan?

716
00:48:58,377 --> 00:48:59,846
- Oh, oh.
- Irish.

717
00:48:59,879 --> 00:49:01,648
Sorry, Tommy.
Sorry, buddy.

718
00:49:04,618 --> 00:49:06,085
Sorry.

719
00:49:06,119 --> 00:49:08,688
I hate you hanging out
with those skanky girls.

720
00:49:17,063 --> 00:49:20,934
I'm... totally numb
on painkillers.

721
00:49:22,936 --> 00:49:24,604
We'll see about that.

722
00:49:30,710 --> 00:49:33,579
- Yeah, you know.
- It's a weird one.

723
00:49:36,149 --> 00:49:39,118
Sammy.
What are you doing here?

724
00:49:39,152 --> 00:49:41,154
Uh, I was invited.

725
00:49:41,187 --> 00:49:43,589
- You're coming with me.
- No, I'm not.

726
00:50:03,276 --> 00:50:05,912
Yeah, but you're not into her,
are you?

727
00:50:05,945 --> 00:50:06,913
Dude, she's 15.

728
00:50:06,946 --> 00:50:09,916
Believe me, mate, I know.
I'm copping hell.

729
00:50:09,949 --> 00:50:12,385
You wouldn't go there, right?

730
00:50:12,418 --> 00:50:15,021
Mate, she just likes
hanging out.

731
00:50:15,054 --> 00:50:16,322
It's harmless.

732
00:50:18,091 --> 00:50:20,626
Okay. Come on, mate.
Give me five more.

733
00:50:24,798 --> 00:50:28,334
Tommy, Chang's boys,
Scott and Glenn. All grown up.

734
00:50:28,367 --> 00:50:29,803
- How are you?
- Hello.

735
00:50:29,836 --> 00:50:31,404
- How you doin', mate?
- Hey.

736
00:50:31,437 --> 00:50:34,307
I remember you.
You played for Dad.

737
00:50:34,340 --> 00:50:35,441
Yeah.

738
00:50:35,474 --> 00:50:37,643
1998 to 2003, yeah?

739
00:50:38,778 --> 00:50:40,814
Dad loved you.

740
00:50:40,847 --> 00:50:42,348
Yeah, he'll be...
He'll be missed.

741
00:50:42,381 --> 00:50:44,083
Especially on Saturday.

742
00:50:46,085 --> 00:50:49,022
Well, at least
you've got Nick here.

743
00:50:49,055 --> 00:50:51,424
Oh, I'm an assistant,
not the coach.

744
00:50:52,258 --> 00:50:53,993
You're kidding, right?

745
00:51:04,203 --> 00:51:06,005
You gotta step up.

746
00:51:06,039 --> 00:51:07,373
Okay.

747
00:51:07,406 --> 00:51:10,443
I'll step up if you and Morts
are my assistants.

748
00:51:32,098 --> 00:51:34,433
I am sorry.

749
00:51:34,467 --> 00:51:36,402
Really, I am sorry.

750
00:51:40,373 --> 00:51:43,342
Yeah, I know, mate.

751
00:51:43,376 --> 00:51:47,180
No, you don't.
I apologized.

752
00:51:47,213 --> 00:51:49,015
We shook hands.

753
00:51:49,048 --> 00:51:51,284
Said we'd be mates.

754
00:51:53,987 --> 00:51:56,756
Haven't spoken since.

755
00:52:01,961 --> 00:52:04,097
- What?
- No.

756
00:52:04,130 --> 00:52:07,867
Chicks are right, you know?

757
00:52:07,901 --> 00:52:10,036
Guys are bloody hopeless.

758
00:52:14,573 --> 00:52:16,509
Hey, you wanna have a kick?

759
00:52:22,148 --> 00:52:24,317
You remember
where the lights are?

760
00:52:24,350 --> 00:52:26,152
I reckon we can find 'em.

761
00:52:32,225 --> 00:52:35,528
Evening, ladies!

762
00:52:35,561 --> 00:52:37,096
Oh, Franky!

763
00:52:40,333 --> 00:52:42,201
Somebody order a cocktail?

764
00:53:02,488 --> 00:53:04,257
Oh!

765
00:53:04,290 --> 00:53:05,258
Oh-ho-ho!

766
00:53:05,291 --> 00:53:07,894
Tom's still got it!

767
00:53:07,927 --> 00:53:08,995
Tommy!

768
00:53:09,028 --> 00:53:10,396
I'm not getting that!

769
00:53:10,429 --> 00:53:12,165
Franky, it's your turn, buddy.

770
00:53:12,198 --> 00:53:13,867
Normally I would, but...

771
00:53:13,900 --> 00:53:16,602
I think I pulled a hammy
delivering that bullet pass.

772
00:53:16,635 --> 00:53:18,872
I'll get it.

773
00:53:18,905 --> 00:53:20,940
Oh, I gotta stop having
Midori and milk.

774
00:53:20,974 --> 00:53:23,476
Ohh!

775
00:53:23,509 --> 00:53:26,846
Welcome to Ron Evans Oval
down here in Portarlington,

776
00:53:26,880 --> 00:53:28,214
A club steeped in rich history.

777
00:53:28,247 --> 00:53:30,950
The only team playing better
than the Tigers this year

778
00:53:30,984 --> 00:53:32,318
Is the Demons.

779
00:53:32,351 --> 00:53:34,320
The winner will go straight
through to the Grand Final

780
00:53:34,353 --> 00:53:37,256
And, of course,
get the all-important week off.

781
00:53:37,290 --> 00:53:40,359
Peters with the quick tap,
but the Tigers move it forward.

782
00:53:40,393 --> 00:53:42,595
Dawson out with a strong mark.

783
00:53:42,628 --> 00:53:45,999
Plays it off to Dunn.
Dunn with a kick inside 50.

784
00:53:46,032 --> 00:53:47,867
A bouncing ball to Tanner.

785
00:53:47,901 --> 00:53:50,970
Franky runs around,
this-a-away, that-a-away,

786
00:53:51,004 --> 00:53:52,605
And all of a sudden
he's caught.

787
00:53:52,638 --> 00:53:55,041
He took far too long.
Brown's got him.

788
00:53:55,074 --> 00:53:57,010
Anderson runs off.
He's quick too.

789
00:53:57,043 --> 00:54:00,013
One bounce and kicks it
out of defense.

790
00:54:00,046 --> 00:54:01,480
The ball spills
out of the back.

791
00:54:01,514 --> 00:54:03,516
The extra man, Harvey,
picks it up, steps.

792
00:54:03,549 --> 00:54:04,583
It's a goal!

793
00:54:04,617 --> 00:54:07,253
It's a cheapie,
but doesn't he love it.

794
00:54:07,286 --> 00:54:10,189
He loves to chat as well.

795
00:54:10,223 --> 00:54:11,190
See you, Dunny!

796
00:54:13,392 --> 00:54:15,394
Jack Didier
handball to Tommy Dunn.

797
00:54:15,395 --> 00:54:17,297
Dunn with the quick reply.

798
00:54:17,330 --> 00:54:19,265
And what a great comeback year
Dunn is having.

799
00:54:19,299 --> 00:54:21,968
He's probably leading
the Tigers' best and fairest.

800
00:54:22,002 --> 00:54:24,971
At 3/4 time, Portarlington
have a strong lead.

801
00:54:25,005 --> 00:54:26,339
Tigers will need to lift.

802
00:54:26,372 --> 00:54:28,508
I want next Saturday off!

803
00:54:28,541 --> 00:54:31,912
Straight through
to the Grand Final.

804
00:54:31,945 --> 00:54:34,414
Switch to man-on-man.

805
00:54:34,416 --> 00:54:35,918
Pile on the forward pressure.

806
00:54:35,951 --> 00:54:38,020
I want three tackles
out of each of you.

807
00:54:38,053 --> 00:54:39,121
- Right?
- Yes!

808
00:54:39,154 --> 00:54:40,189
Let's do this!

809
00:54:40,222 --> 00:54:41,556
Go on!

810
00:54:44,894 --> 00:54:46,996
Hey.

811
00:54:47,029 --> 00:54:48,397
Tag 17.

812
00:54:48,430 --> 00:54:49,531
He's killing us.

813
00:54:49,564 --> 00:54:53,002
Get physical with him.
Go on.

814
00:54:53,035 --> 00:54:54,436
Dunn given the huge assignment

815
00:54:54,469 --> 00:54:56,371
To quell the influence of the
Demons' best footer, Harvey,

816
00:54:56,405 --> 00:54:58,440
If the Tigers are to have
any chance of victory

817
00:54:58,473 --> 00:54:59,574
And the coveted week off.

818
00:54:59,608 --> 00:55:00,709
Robbo with the tap.

819
00:55:00,742 --> 00:55:02,644
Didier sharks it,
handballs it to Dunn.

820
00:55:02,677 --> 00:55:05,447
A pack forms. Players rummaging
at ground level.

821
00:55:05,480 --> 00:55:08,017
The boundary throw-in.
Robbo down to Dunn.

822
00:55:08,050 --> 00:55:10,652
A fierce tackle from Farrell.
Demons on the rebound.

823
00:55:10,685 --> 00:55:12,221
Ball bouncing down
to the pocket.

824
00:55:12,254 --> 00:55:13,923
Great shepherd from Irish!

825
00:55:13,956 --> 00:55:16,125
Allows Tanner to wheel around
on his right foot,

826
00:55:16,158 --> 00:55:17,492
Slots it through.

827
00:55:17,526 --> 00:55:18,527
First we've seen
of Tanner today.

828
00:55:18,560 --> 00:55:20,462
He's been very quiet,
the big fella.

829
00:55:20,495 --> 00:55:22,631
Robbo off
the Nicky Reagan fumble.

830
00:55:22,664 --> 00:55:25,400
Recovers well.
Kicks long to the forward line.

831
00:55:25,434 --> 00:55:27,469
And out comes Mortimer!

832
00:55:27,502 --> 00:55:30,372
A strong mark.

833
00:55:30,405 --> 00:55:32,541
From 40 meters out,
lines it up purposely

834
00:55:32,574 --> 00:55:34,543
And slots it through.

835
00:55:34,576 --> 00:55:36,211
Another nice goal
from Mortimer.

836
00:55:36,245 --> 00:55:38,613
The Tigers are back in this.

837
00:55:38,647 --> 00:55:39,714
Tanner picks up the crumb,

838
00:55:39,748 --> 00:55:40,815
Tries to crash his way
through the pack.

839
00:55:40,849 --> 00:55:43,652
Can't do it.
Mugsy Ryan pulls him down.

840
00:55:43,685 --> 00:55:46,621
- Ugly by name, ugly by nature.
- Bloody hell.

841
00:55:46,655 --> 00:55:50,125
Harvey and Dunn jostle for
position in the goal square,

842
00:55:50,159 --> 00:55:51,460
Both using their bodies.

843
00:55:51,493 --> 00:55:53,162
Oh, it's over the back.

844
00:55:53,195 --> 00:55:56,131
Harvey, strong goal.

845
00:55:56,165 --> 00:55:58,267
By my calculations,
that's number seven.

846
00:55:58,300 --> 00:56:01,470
And Harvey, there's a crush.
Pushes Tommy Dunn in the back.

847
00:56:01,503 --> 00:56:04,606
Seven big ones. He's killed
Dunn in the last quarter.

848
00:56:04,639 --> 00:56:07,576
He has pulled his proverbial
stripes down.

849
00:56:07,609 --> 00:56:09,611
The Demons are running away
with this one.

850
00:56:09,644 --> 00:56:12,281
The Tigers are gonna have
to play a lot better next week

851
00:56:12,314 --> 00:56:15,384
To earn a spot in their
second consecutive Grand Final.

852
00:56:22,424 --> 00:56:24,259
Oh, here he is.

853
00:56:24,293 --> 00:56:26,061
Hey, great tag today, mate.

854
00:56:26,095 --> 00:56:29,664
You really shut me down
out there.

855
00:56:29,698 --> 00:56:32,501
No, I really hope
you ladies win next week.

856
00:56:32,534 --> 00:56:34,436
I'd love to see you
in the granny.

857
00:56:34,469 --> 00:56:36,471
Oh, that's if you get picked
for the team, that is.

858
00:56:38,207 --> 00:56:39,975
Tommy...

859
00:56:40,009 --> 00:56:42,677
Tommy!

860
00:56:42,711 --> 00:56:45,547
You don't want to get pumped
twice in one day, do you?

861
00:56:47,216 --> 00:56:48,550
♪ Yellow and black

862
00:56:48,583 --> 00:56:50,652
♪ Yes, we're from Tigerland

863
00:56:50,685 --> 00:56:52,421
You'll get him next time.

864
00:56:52,454 --> 00:56:55,757
Won't be a next time
if I don't get picked.

865
00:56:55,790 --> 00:56:58,093
What happened?

866
00:56:58,127 --> 00:57:00,195
Played like shite.

867
00:57:00,229 --> 00:57:02,998
Oh, well.
The world still turns.

868
00:57:03,032 --> 00:57:05,400
It was a semifinal.

869
00:57:14,676 --> 00:57:16,645
Welcome
to the Preliminary Final.

870
00:57:16,678 --> 00:57:20,149
We're playing here at Anglesea,
home to the Anglesea Kangaroos.

871
00:57:20,182 --> 00:57:22,517
The winner of this game is
bound for the Grand Final.

872
00:57:22,551 --> 00:57:24,086
Instant elimination
for the loser.

873
00:57:24,119 --> 00:57:26,121
Here we go.

874
00:57:26,155 --> 00:57:28,557
And the ball's up in the air.
Engel sends the tap to Stevens.

875
00:57:28,590 --> 00:57:31,493
Dunn takes him down.
To Mills. Hesitates.

876
00:57:31,526 --> 00:57:33,295
Irish and Dawson
bring him down.

877
00:57:33,328 --> 00:57:35,097
A great gang tackle.

878
00:57:35,130 --> 00:57:36,131
Evans tries to clear.

879
00:57:36,165 --> 00:57:39,368
Great smother, Tommy Dunn.

880
00:57:39,401 --> 00:57:40,435
Reagan, a quick handball
to Dunn.

881
00:57:40,469 --> 00:57:43,338
Dunn wheels around
on his right foot.

882
00:57:43,372 --> 00:57:46,508
And Franky Tanner
takes a great mark.

883
00:57:46,541 --> 00:57:47,742
Déjà vu for Edwards.

884
00:57:47,776 --> 00:57:50,045
He had a nightmare
in last year's Grand Final,

885
00:57:50,079 --> 00:57:51,346
And Franky's
doing it to him again.

886
00:57:51,380 --> 00:57:53,515
You like that?
Sammy, come here.

887
00:57:55,517 --> 00:57:58,353
Chelsea, Chelsea, Chelsea,
wait up, wait up.

888
00:57:58,387 --> 00:58:00,122
As long as you're
writing down numbers.

889
00:58:00,155 --> 00:58:01,623
I don't know.

890
00:58:01,656 --> 00:58:03,792
- Call me anytime, yeah.
- Really?

891
00:58:03,825 --> 00:58:05,694
Really, yeah

892
00:58:05,727 --> 00:58:09,198
You're the only goal
I haven't scored.

893
00:58:09,231 --> 00:58:11,066
Irish slides on the ground.
Tap to Dunn.

894
00:58:11,100 --> 00:58:14,303
Dunn to Reagan.
Nicky Reagan.

895
00:58:14,336 --> 00:58:17,372
And Tanner again with
superb body movement

896
00:58:17,406 --> 00:58:18,540
Has taken a strong mark.

897
00:58:18,573 --> 00:58:21,376
Lines up from an angle
and slots it through.

898
00:58:21,410 --> 00:58:22,277
There's no stopping the

899
00:58:22,311 --> 00:58:25,080
Vaudeville act
here this afternoon.

900
00:58:25,114 --> 00:58:26,548
Morts comes in
off the boundary.

901
00:58:26,581 --> 00:58:29,418
Edwards taken down.
Dawson swoops. Goal!

902
00:58:29,451 --> 00:58:30,752
Great tackle for Morts.

903
00:58:30,785 --> 00:58:32,821
Allowed Dawson to swoop
and convert it.

904
00:58:32,854 --> 00:58:35,224
Torquay has full control
of this game.

905
00:58:35,257 --> 00:58:36,791
Tommy Dunn running down the
wing, looks up.

906
00:58:36,825 --> 00:58:39,428
Kicks. Out on the full.
A shocking kick.

907
00:58:39,461 --> 00:58:41,696
Half the thought of missing out
on Grand Final selection again

908
00:58:41,730 --> 00:58:43,532
Could be weighing heavily
upon him.

909
00:58:43,565 --> 00:58:46,301
He's had a great year, but not
a great Finals campaign.

910
00:58:48,203 --> 00:58:51,206
Center bounce.
Robbo with the tap.

911
00:58:51,240 --> 00:58:54,376
Stevens the other way.
The old one-two with Mills.

912
00:58:54,409 --> 00:58:56,478
Mills, the handball
back to Stevens.

913
00:58:56,511 --> 00:58:57,779
Stevens kick... Coppola!

914
00:58:57,812 --> 00:59:01,216
Unselfishly handballs
into an open goal by Anglesea.

915
00:59:01,250 --> 00:59:02,717
A great team goal.

916
00:59:02,751 --> 00:59:05,620
Boundary throw-in.
Pats it down.

917
00:59:05,654 --> 00:59:09,658
Great snap.
Another one for Francis Ford.

918
00:59:09,691 --> 00:59:10,859
Dunn attacks the ball.

919
00:59:10,892 --> 00:59:12,894
Oh, Fitz is down!
They come from everywhere.

920
00:59:12,927 --> 00:59:15,597
I'm sure he was going the ball,
but it didn't look great.

921
00:59:15,630 --> 00:59:17,266
A 50-meter penalty.

922
00:59:17,299 --> 00:59:19,501
Chang's not gonna be happy
with that.

923
00:59:19,534 --> 00:59:20,902
Another goal to Anglesea.

924
00:59:20,935 --> 00:59:24,239
A great effort to get up and
take that hit by Fitzgerald.

925
00:59:24,273 --> 00:59:26,141
The ball's up...

926
00:59:26,175 --> 00:59:29,711
Siren time. That's it.
The Tigers have done it.

927
00:59:29,744 --> 00:59:32,314
They were hungry for this one.

928
00:59:33,915 --> 00:59:37,219
We're going to the big dance,
Charlie.

929
00:59:37,252 --> 00:59:39,354
Congratulations.
Ha

930
00:59:45,960 --> 00:59:47,696
All right. Forwards:

931
00:59:47,729 --> 00:59:51,600
Knights, Mortimer,

932
00:59:51,633 --> 00:59:53,502
Milkey,

933
00:59:53,535 --> 00:59:55,237
Tanner,

934
00:59:55,270 --> 00:59:57,639
Young, Barry.

935
00:59:57,672 --> 01:00:01,276
Followers: Robbo...

936
01:00:01,310 --> 01:00:05,414
Reagan, Pitcher,

937
01:00:05,447 --> 01:00:07,382
And Dunn.

938
01:00:09,951 --> 01:00:12,421
Interchange...

939
01:00:12,454 --> 01:00:13,688
Yeah, you said it.

940
01:00:13,722 --> 01:00:15,324
Hey, Tommy.

941
01:00:16,491 --> 01:00:18,393
I'll see you at Franky's.

942
01:00:19,494 --> 01:00:20,695
Thanks, Chang.

943
01:00:20,729 --> 01:00:23,798
I didn't do you any favors, son.

944
01:00:23,832 --> 01:00:26,835
You proved yourself.

945
01:00:26,868 --> 01:00:29,604
You better stop that prick
next week, though.

946
01:00:30,772 --> 01:00:32,607
All right.

947
01:00:32,641 --> 01:00:34,843
No pressure.

948
01:00:38,547 --> 01:00:41,283
Hey, another big one
this weekend, Nick?

949
01:00:41,316 --> 01:00:42,717
Yeah.

950
01:00:42,751 --> 01:00:45,587
You gotta coach 'em, Nicky.

951
01:00:45,620 --> 01:00:48,323
Yeah, I said I would...

952
01:00:48,357 --> 01:00:50,759
If Tommy and Morts
were assistants.

953
01:00:50,792 --> 01:00:53,528
What about me, you dog?

954
01:00:53,562 --> 01:00:56,931
I need an extra hand
running water, too?

955
01:00:57,632 --> 01:00:59,200
Yeah, I'm up.

956
01:01:01,503 --> 01:01:03,605
Yeah, all right, me too.

957
01:01:03,638 --> 01:01:05,540
You dogs.

958
01:01:05,574 --> 01:01:07,342
Training tomorrow at eight.

959
01:01:07,376 --> 01:01:08,777
Eight?

960
01:01:08,810 --> 01:01:12,681
Hey, does anyone know
where Rose lives?

961
01:01:15,917 --> 01:01:18,620
- Why do you ask?
- Is that a no?

962
01:01:18,653 --> 01:01:20,455
- No, don't go there, mate.
- After you, Coach.

963
01:01:20,489 --> 01:01:22,257
I believe you.

964
01:01:44,546 --> 01:01:46,481
Uh, hi.

965
01:01:46,515 --> 01:01:47,916
Hi.

966
01:01:49,618 --> 01:01:52,487
I was looking for Rose.

967
01:01:52,521 --> 01:01:57,792
She moved out years ago.
She's on Vine, number 14.

968
01:01:57,826 --> 01:01:59,828
Okay. All right.

969
01:01:59,861 --> 01:02:00,829
Thanks.

970
01:02:00,862 --> 01:02:02,897
Hey, uh...

971
01:02:02,931 --> 01:02:05,734
I saw you at the ceremony.

972
01:02:05,767 --> 01:02:07,469
It's good you came back for it.

973
01:02:10,905 --> 01:02:13,908
Tom, would you come in
for a minute?

974
01:02:13,942 --> 01:02:16,745
- I have to get going.
- Just for a minute?

975
01:02:27,622 --> 01:02:30,525
Dad's asleep.
Don't have to worry.

976
01:02:30,559 --> 01:02:32,494
Why would I be worried?

977
01:02:32,527 --> 01:02:33,662
No, I mean...

978
01:02:36,865 --> 01:02:39,401
You still live here?

979
01:02:39,434 --> 01:02:40,234
Just moved back from Melbourne.

980
01:02:40,268 --> 01:02:43,004
I finished Uni,
and Dad's been sick.

981
01:02:46,841 --> 01:02:49,511
Look, it's...

982
01:02:49,544 --> 01:02:51,846
It's nice to see you,
but I should really get going.

983
01:02:51,880 --> 01:02:54,449
Maybe another time then.
Not here, but we could...

984
01:02:54,483 --> 01:02:58,720
Listen, you seem to be
doing great, but, um...

985
01:02:58,753 --> 01:03:00,755
I have to go.

986
01:03:20,809 --> 01:03:22,076
Hi.

987
01:03:26,748 --> 01:03:28,417
How'd you get this address?

988
01:03:28,450 --> 01:03:33,788
I went to your old house.
Sammy gave it to me.

989
01:03:33,822 --> 01:03:36,024
You saw Sammy?

990
01:03:41,029 --> 01:03:45,434
What are you doing here, Tom?

991
01:03:45,467 --> 01:03:46,167
I was just hanging out
with the boys.

992
01:03:46,200 --> 01:03:49,704
- Are you drunk?
- No. What?

993
01:03:49,738 --> 01:03:54,075
You know, you and I...

994
01:03:57,712 --> 01:03:59,514
We would never have...

995
01:04:01,082 --> 01:04:03,051
We were kids.

996
01:04:04,786 --> 01:04:07,756
Look, I never left.

997
01:04:07,789 --> 01:04:09,591
I haven't gotten anywhere.

998
01:04:09,624 --> 01:04:11,993
- What? That's fine.
- I'm not doing what I planned.

999
01:04:12,026 --> 01:04:15,964
But you know what?
I'm happy.

1000
01:04:15,997 --> 01:04:16,631
Great.

1001
01:04:16,665 --> 01:04:17,932
You're happy.

1002
01:04:26,140 --> 01:04:28,076
I've moved on.

1003
01:04:55,704 --> 01:04:58,039
You know, I ran into
Cowboy's mom last week.

1004
01:04:58,072 --> 01:05:01,943
She told me that for so long...

1005
01:05:01,976 --> 01:05:04,245
She didn't understand football.

1006
01:05:04,278 --> 01:05:07,716
When Cowboy was a kid, he was
out every night, every weekend,

1007
01:05:07,749 --> 01:05:10,485
Out in the field
kicking around a ball.

1008
01:05:10,519 --> 01:05:12,186
"My son could be doing more
with his life."

1009
01:05:12,220 --> 01:05:13,788
That's what she thought.

1010
01:05:13,822 --> 01:05:18,092
It wasn't until
she lost Cowboy...

1011
01:05:18,126 --> 01:05:20,061
In the accident.

1012
01:05:22,196 --> 01:05:24,966
And an abundance of players...

1013
01:05:24,999 --> 01:05:28,503
Good, caring, driven blokes...

1014
01:05:28,537 --> 01:05:30,905
There were lots of you,
she said,

1015
01:05:30,939 --> 01:05:34,175
Came out of the woodwork,

1016
01:05:34,208 --> 01:05:35,877
Gave her a hand,

1017
01:05:35,910 --> 01:05:39,814
Fixing up the car,
bringing in the shopping,

1018
01:05:39,848 --> 01:05:44,619
Sharing a yarn about her son.

1019
01:05:44,653 --> 01:05:46,855
It wasn't until then

1020
01:05:46,888 --> 01:05:50,124
That she appreciated
what football's about.

1021
01:05:50,158 --> 01:05:52,193
When his teammates started
to behave like a family,

1022
01:05:52,226 --> 01:05:56,297
She realized that her son...

1023
01:05:56,330 --> 01:06:00,802
Was part of something more.

1024
01:06:00,835 --> 01:06:04,038
He was part of a team.

1025
01:06:04,072 --> 01:06:06,708
Cowboy was tough.

1026
01:06:06,741 --> 01:06:09,711
There were none tougher.

1027
01:06:09,744 --> 01:06:12,313
He concentrated...

1028
01:06:12,346 --> 01:06:16,150
For four quarters every game.

1029
01:06:16,184 --> 01:06:21,690
He was at the bottom of the pack
every time there was a contest.

1030
01:06:21,723 --> 01:06:26,127
He tackled with intent
every time.

1031
01:06:26,160 --> 01:06:28,763
And if there was a blue,
he was always at your back.

1032
01:06:28,797 --> 01:06:32,200
You could count on it.

1033
01:06:32,233 --> 01:06:33,401
And most of the time
he was doing that

1034
01:06:33,434 --> 01:06:38,072
With a dislocated shoulder
or a couple of broken fingers.

1035
01:06:40,274 --> 01:06:44,979
He typified courage.

1036
01:06:45,013 --> 01:06:47,982
He was tough.
He was Cowboy tough.

1037
01:06:48,016 --> 01:06:50,151
And that's what I want
from you today.

1038
01:06:50,184 --> 01:06:55,023
I want every one of you
to be bloody Cowboy tough.

1039
01:06:55,056 --> 01:06:58,159
They all know the game plan.
I've talked to you individually.

1040
01:06:58,192 --> 01:07:00,795
We man up tight
when they've got the pill.

1041
01:07:00,829 --> 01:07:03,131
You break off fast
and make a play

1042
01:07:03,164 --> 01:07:04,966
As soon as there's a turnover,

1043
01:07:04,999 --> 01:07:09,638
And we force those turnovers
with ferocious bloody tackling.

1044
01:07:09,671 --> 01:07:12,140
Right, I want you all
to take a seat. Come on.

1045
01:07:12,173 --> 01:07:13,842
Boys, bring it in
nice and tight.

1046
01:07:13,875 --> 01:07:15,677
Watertight, watertight.

1047
01:07:15,710 --> 01:07:18,713
Pull up a bit of floor.
Keep it quiet.

1048
01:07:18,747 --> 01:07:20,381
I want you to close your eyes.

1049
01:07:20,414 --> 01:07:23,685
Go on, close your eyes.

1050
01:07:23,718 --> 01:07:26,387
I want you to imagine something.

1051
01:07:26,420 --> 01:07:28,256
Picture this:

1052
01:07:28,289 --> 01:07:30,024
A mother.

1053
01:07:30,058 --> 01:07:31,392
Your mother.

1054
01:07:31,425 --> 01:07:32,994
Could be your sister.

1055
01:07:33,027 --> 01:07:36,831
Anyone who's brought a child
into the world.

1056
01:07:36,865 --> 01:07:38,733
Picture that child.

1057
01:07:40,268 --> 01:07:43,104
Little face.

1058
01:07:43,137 --> 01:07:45,273
A smile.

1059
01:07:45,306 --> 01:07:46,407
The happiness.

1060
01:07:46,440 --> 01:07:49,377
Now picture
some vicious bastard

1061
01:07:49,410 --> 01:07:51,846
Who wants to take
that child off her.

1062
01:07:51,880 --> 01:07:54,082
He's pushed her,

1063
01:07:54,115 --> 01:07:56,985
He's backhanded her in the face,

1064
01:07:57,018 --> 01:08:00,321
And he is trying
to take that child.

1065
01:08:00,354 --> 01:08:01,690
Can you picture that?

1066
01:08:01,723 --> 01:08:03,291
Yes.

1067
01:08:03,324 --> 01:08:05,293
There is no way

1068
01:08:05,326 --> 01:08:08,763
That she's going to let him
take that child.

1069
01:08:08,797 --> 01:08:11,199
She will find an inner strength,

1070
01:08:11,232 --> 01:08:14,035
A mental strength
she never knew she had.

1071
01:08:14,068 --> 01:08:17,305
She's going to fight
tooth and nail.

1072
01:08:17,338 --> 01:08:21,776
She will die rather than let
that bastard take that child,

1073
01:08:21,810 --> 01:08:25,980
And she will not lose.

1074
01:08:26,014 --> 01:08:27,949
You've seen it
in the animal world,

1075
01:08:27,982 --> 01:08:30,051
And it's in our world too.

1076
01:08:30,084 --> 01:08:32,687
A superhuman strength.

1077
01:08:32,721 --> 01:08:35,690
I want you to take that strength

1078
01:08:35,724 --> 01:08:39,861
And get out there
and rip this game apart!

1079
01:08:39,894 --> 01:08:41,462
Have you got it in you?

1080
01:08:41,495 --> 01:08:43,397
- Yes, sir!
- Get out there!

1081
01:08:56,778 --> 01:08:59,213
Welcome to Spring Creek Reserve
in Torquay,

1082
01:08:59,247 --> 01:09:02,050
The scene for today's
2003 Grand Final

1083
01:09:02,083 --> 01:09:04,152
Between archenemies
the Torquay Tigers

1084
01:09:04,185 --> 01:09:06,955
And the Portarlington Demons.

1085
01:09:06,988 --> 01:09:09,490
The Torquay fans will be eager
to see their side

1086
01:09:09,523 --> 01:09:12,093
Win their first-ever
back-to-back premiership.

1087
01:09:12,126 --> 01:09:14,095
But I gotta tell you what.
From my observation,

1088
01:09:14,128 --> 01:09:15,897
These Demons have looked
harder and faster

1089
01:09:15,930 --> 01:09:17,832
And the better side all year.

1090
01:09:17,866 --> 01:09:19,801
Well, certainly these young
Tigers have earned it, Sam.

1091
01:09:23,037 --> 01:09:26,007
Tommy Dunn runs to Harvey.
A bit of a surprise move,

1092
01:09:26,040 --> 01:09:29,310
Considering the toweling that
Harvey gave Dunn two weeks ago,

1093
01:09:29,343 --> 01:09:30,611
But Chang's backed his man.

1094
01:09:30,644 --> 01:09:34,082
The bounce. Robbo with the tap,
but only as far as Riggs.

1095
01:09:34,115 --> 01:09:37,786
Harvey gets the handball.
Dunn with a great tackle!

1096
01:09:37,819 --> 01:09:40,354
What an important start
for Tommy Dunn.

1097
01:09:40,388 --> 01:09:41,489
The ball up in the air.

1098
01:09:41,522 --> 01:09:44,025
Irish runs onto it,
runs for the middle.

1099
01:09:44,058 --> 01:09:46,027
Puts boot to ball.
A long kick.

1100
01:09:46,060 --> 01:09:50,932
And Tanner with great poise
and positioning takes the mark.

1101
01:09:50,965 --> 01:09:53,868
Lines it up directly in front,
and he goals.

1102
01:09:53,902 --> 01:09:56,504
First point for the Tigers.
What a ripping start.

1103
01:09:56,537 --> 01:09:58,339
And don't they just
love him here?

1104
01:09:58,372 --> 01:10:00,408
He has folk hero status.

1105
01:10:00,441 --> 01:10:01,976
The bouncing ball
in the square.

1106
01:10:02,010 --> 01:10:04,112
Dawson with a scissor kick.
Goal!

1107
01:10:07,248 --> 01:10:09,183
Back in the center,
Farrell down to Riggs,

1108
01:10:09,217 --> 01:10:11,219
Back to Farrell,
quickly to Turner.

1109
01:10:11,252 --> 01:10:13,421
Quick kick into
the forward line. Anderson!

1110
01:10:15,056 --> 01:10:16,858
The ball up,
15 meters out.

1111
01:10:16,891 --> 01:10:18,359
Campbell reaching up the pack,
snaps.

1112
01:10:18,392 --> 01:10:21,095
A goal!
The Demons are fighting back.

1113
01:10:24,298 --> 01:10:27,068
The ball loose in the pocket.
Handball comes out to Harding.

1114
01:10:27,101 --> 01:10:29,070
Dunn manhandles him
out of the way.

1115
01:10:29,103 --> 01:10:30,171
Handballs to Tanner.

1116
01:10:30,204 --> 01:10:32,040
Franky steps another goal.

1117
01:10:32,073 --> 01:10:34,809
The Tigers celebrate.

1118
01:10:34,843 --> 01:10:38,079
Yeah!

1119
01:10:38,112 --> 01:10:39,981
Harvey battles for position,
handballs to Campbell.

1120
01:10:40,014 --> 01:10:42,851
Campbell bursts through
the center, takes one bounce.

1121
01:10:44,452 --> 01:10:46,320
Oh, Anderson
at the back, steps.

1122
01:10:46,354 --> 01:10:48,289
Goal. Demons take the front.

1123
01:10:52,126 --> 01:10:54,028
Running hard,
Dawson finds Reagan.

1124
01:10:54,062 --> 01:10:55,997
Blind turns,
presses through a pack.

1125
01:10:56,030 --> 01:10:57,265
Reagan gets the handball
up to Irish.

1126
01:10:57,298 --> 01:10:59,100
Irish kicks long.

1127
01:10:59,133 --> 01:11:02,871
Mortimer! What a courageous
mark by Mortimer.

1128
01:11:02,904 --> 01:11:04,438
Lines it up and goal.

1129
01:11:10,411 --> 01:11:12,613
The ball up on the square.
Robbo taps it down.

1130
01:11:12,646 --> 01:11:15,083
Gibbs pounces on the ball,
falls to Didier,

1131
01:11:15,116 --> 01:11:18,352
Over to Bishop, finds Irish,
back inside to Dunn.

1132
01:11:18,386 --> 01:11:20,488
He's run strongly.
Inside 50.

1133
01:11:20,521 --> 01:11:23,624
Franky Tanner presents himself
and takes a strong mark.

1134
01:11:23,657 --> 01:11:25,326
Great play by the Tigers.

1135
01:11:25,359 --> 01:11:26,627
Tanner's having
a field day today.

1136
01:11:26,660 --> 01:11:29,063
That's the aggression he needs
to bring for the Tigers

1137
01:11:29,097 --> 01:11:31,532
To be able to win the big one.

1138
01:11:31,565 --> 01:11:32,733
The bounce down.

1139
01:11:32,766 --> 01:11:35,236
Farrell down to Gibbs,
to Foley, back to Gibbs.

1140
01:11:35,269 --> 01:11:37,305
1-2 to Frawley.

1141
01:11:37,338 --> 01:11:38,406
Frawley kicks long.

1142
01:11:38,439 --> 01:11:40,909
Harvey lurking at the back.

1143
01:11:40,942 --> 01:11:45,046
Harvey on a chest,
takes a mark and goals.

1144
01:11:45,079 --> 01:11:46,547
Harvey hasn't made
a strong today,

1145
01:11:46,580 --> 01:11:48,516
But the Demons
are leading the way.

1146
01:11:48,549 --> 01:11:52,153
They celebrate, the Demons,
a two-goal lead nevertheless.

1147
01:11:54,288 --> 01:11:55,356
Reagan shepherds Harvey out.

1148
01:11:55,389 --> 01:11:56,958
Dunn bolts from the back line.

1149
01:11:56,991 --> 01:11:58,392
Another strong shepherd
from the Tigers.

1150
01:11:58,426 --> 01:12:00,161
Dunn kicks. Finds Dawson.

1151
01:12:00,194 --> 01:12:03,364
Dawson runs in.
Tommy's run on.

1152
01:12:03,397 --> 01:12:04,465
Dunn slots another goal.

1153
01:12:04,498 --> 01:12:06,334
This is the best we've seen
for years.

1154
01:12:06,367 --> 01:12:08,469
Gut-busting run
from Tommy Dunn.

1155
01:12:08,502 --> 01:12:10,138
But the Demons
hold a three-goal lead

1156
01:12:10,171 --> 01:12:11,940
Going into the 3/4 time.

1157
01:12:14,608 --> 01:12:16,177
Do you want to remember
this moment?

1158
01:12:16,210 --> 01:12:17,511
Yes!

1159
01:12:17,545 --> 01:12:19,347
Do you want to be able
to tell your kids

1160
01:12:19,380 --> 01:12:20,681
What you did out there today?

1161
01:12:20,714 --> 01:12:22,083
Yes!

1162
01:12:22,116 --> 01:12:24,418
Unselfish acts.

1163
01:12:24,452 --> 01:12:26,420
That's what I want.

1164
01:12:26,454 --> 01:12:30,058
What price are you
prepared to pay

1165
01:12:30,091 --> 01:12:32,961
To win back-to-back flags?

1166
01:12:32,994 --> 01:12:36,965
Write yourself into the history
of this great club.

1167
01:12:36,998 --> 01:12:37,665
Can you do it?

1168
01:12:37,698 --> 01:12:39,133
Yes!

1169
01:12:39,167 --> 01:12:41,602
Give me everything!

1170
01:12:43,037 --> 01:12:45,206
We believe in you!

1171
01:12:45,239 --> 01:12:47,141
They have not stepped up
to our level!

1172
01:12:47,175 --> 01:12:50,344
And you know why?
Because we have got it!

1173
01:12:50,378 --> 01:12:54,282
We have got what it takes
to be the premiership team.

1174
01:12:54,315 --> 01:12:55,616
Look at all these people
behind us.

1175
01:12:55,649 --> 01:12:58,186
They are here to see us do it.
Come on!

1176
01:12:58,219 --> 01:13:01,022
Let's get out there, boys!
Come on, boys!

1177
01:13:01,055 --> 01:13:02,556
Nicky Reagan
running at the ball,

1178
01:13:02,590 --> 01:13:06,594
Sits aloft the pack
to take a huge mark.

1179
01:13:06,627 --> 01:13:08,229
The Tigers fans are going nuts.

1180
01:13:08,262 --> 01:13:11,099
Reagan kicks from 40.

1181
01:13:11,132 --> 01:13:13,667
It's good!

1182
01:13:13,701 --> 01:13:16,470
The Tigers are only
one goal down.

1183
01:13:19,140 --> 01:13:21,109
The boundary tap,
the ball straight to Harvey.

1184
01:13:21,142 --> 01:13:22,710
Fends off,
handballs to Coen,

1185
01:13:22,743 --> 01:13:24,979
Feigns a handle,
dodges a tackle.

1186
01:13:25,013 --> 01:13:26,447
Left foot goal!

1187
01:13:26,480 --> 01:13:28,016
Ball bounces in.

1188
01:13:28,049 --> 01:13:29,717
Frawley hesitates. Ooh!

1189
01:13:29,750 --> 01:13:32,453
Tanner's got him from behind!
Great rundown.

1190
01:13:32,486 --> 01:13:35,423
Great desperation from Tanner.

1191
01:13:35,456 --> 01:13:37,425
Tanner directly in front,
kicks, converts.

1192
01:13:37,458 --> 01:13:39,227
Another goal for Franky.

1193
01:13:39,260 --> 01:13:41,595
The Tigers have drawn level.

1194
01:13:41,629 --> 01:13:44,198
Inside five minutes to play.

1195
01:13:44,232 --> 01:13:46,000
The crowd on their feet.

1196
01:13:46,034 --> 01:13:47,101
The ball up in the air.

1197
01:13:47,135 --> 01:13:49,270
Farrell gets a tap
only as far as Reagan.

1198
01:13:49,303 --> 01:13:51,672
Farrell spoils, picks it up,
dishes to Gibbs.

1199
01:13:51,705 --> 01:13:54,508
Gibbs kicks long.
Defensive ball hits the ground.

1200
01:13:54,542 --> 01:13:56,244
Anderson swoops, kicks.

1201
01:13:56,277 --> 01:13:59,513
Another goal to Anderson!

1202
01:13:59,547 --> 01:14:03,117
That's the Demons back on top
by five points, Sam.

1203
01:14:03,151 --> 01:14:04,552
Harvey picks up the loose ball.

1204
01:14:04,585 --> 01:14:06,520
Great tackle!

1205
01:14:06,840 --> 01:14:09,976
Dunn's clearly had the better
of Harvey today.

1206
01:14:14,414 --> 01:14:15,415
Ow!

1207
01:14:16,950 --> 01:14:19,919
It feels really like
next goal will win.

1208
01:14:21,087 --> 01:14:24,358
Tigers need a goal.

1209
01:14:24,391 --> 01:14:29,062
Farrell taps the ball down
to Harvey, and he's away.

1210
01:14:29,475 --> 01:14:32,746
- What's wrong with Tommy?
- I don't know.

1211
01:14:32,779 --> 01:14:34,981
Harvey gets on his bike.
He bolts down the wing.

1212
01:14:35,014 --> 01:14:38,084
He's looking for a teammate,
beckons Riggs to come forward.

1213
01:14:38,117 --> 01:14:40,787
Riggs obliges.
He handballs to Riggs.

1214
01:14:40,820 --> 01:14:42,221
Returns back to Harvey.

1215
01:14:42,255 --> 01:14:43,489
Dunn's sprinting
down the ground,

1216
01:14:43,522 --> 01:14:45,224
But he's miles behind him.

1217
01:14:45,258 --> 01:14:46,592
No one's coming at him.

1218
01:14:46,625 --> 01:14:49,195
Harvey realizes he's got
space galore in front of him.

1219
01:14:49,228 --> 01:14:51,130
Cuts inside 50.

1220
01:14:51,164 --> 01:14:52,999
He's still going,
he's lining it up,

1221
01:14:53,032 --> 01:14:54,300
Gonna try for goal.

1222
01:14:54,333 --> 01:14:56,469
Dunn from nowhere!

1223
01:14:56,502 --> 01:14:58,071
The perfect smother!

1224
01:14:58,104 --> 01:14:59,739
A premiership defining moment.

1225
01:14:59,773 --> 01:15:00,706
Yes!

1226
01:15:00,740 --> 01:15:02,008
Reagan pounces
on the loose ball.

1227
01:15:07,246 --> 01:15:08,481
Reagan on the rebound.

1228
01:15:08,514 --> 01:15:10,183
They're coming in
from everywhere.

1229
01:15:10,216 --> 01:15:12,018
20 seconds left.

1230
01:15:12,051 --> 01:15:13,186
Go, go!

1231
01:15:15,054 --> 01:15:17,991
He takes another bounce.
He feigns a handball.

1232
01:15:18,024 --> 01:15:20,760
He raises his eyes,
looks for a leader forward.

1233
01:15:20,794 --> 01:15:23,897
Mortimer's the obvious target.
He puts foot to ball.

1234
01:15:28,034 --> 01:15:30,203
And Mortimer's got it!
He's got it!

1235
01:15:30,236 --> 01:15:32,906
- Mortimer has got the ball.
- Yes!

1236
01:15:35,875 --> 01:15:37,510
10 seconds left.

1237
01:15:37,543 --> 01:15:40,246
He'll need this goal
for the win.

1238
01:15:44,217 --> 01:15:48,054
It's come down to this.
One last kick.

1239
01:15:48,087 --> 01:15:50,023
What courage from Dunn.

1240
01:15:51,557 --> 01:15:54,393
What pressure on the young man.

1241
01:15:54,427 --> 01:15:56,796
Mortimer, the weight
of the entire club

1242
01:15:56,830 --> 01:15:58,898
On his broad shoulders.

1243
01:15:58,932 --> 01:16:01,167
He comes in, a tight angle.

1244
01:16:01,200 --> 01:16:03,036
Bananas.

1245
01:16:03,069 --> 01:16:05,538
It's a goal! A goal!

1246
01:16:05,571 --> 01:16:08,474
The Tigers win
back-to-back flags.

1247
01:16:08,507 --> 01:16:11,177
The crowd goes nuts!

1248
01:16:11,210 --> 01:16:14,080
The Tigers all run at Mortimer.
They've done it.

1249
01:16:14,113 --> 01:16:17,450
That smother by Tommy Dunn
will go down in history.

1250
01:16:17,483 --> 01:16:18,751
The kids storm the ground,

1251
01:16:18,784 --> 01:16:21,287
And it's pandemonium down here
at Spring Creek, Sam.

1252
01:16:21,320 --> 01:16:23,923
What a comeback from Dunn.

1253
01:16:23,957 --> 01:16:26,893
That smother will go down
in footballing folklore.

1254
01:16:26,926 --> 01:16:28,361
What a famous victory.

1255
01:16:28,394 --> 01:16:31,464
Chang's brought them a second
premiership in as many years.

1256
01:16:34,600 --> 01:16:37,503
They lift Mortimer high,
AFL bound.

1257
01:16:37,536 --> 01:16:39,505
He won't be the only one.

1258
01:16:39,538 --> 01:16:41,975
You'd think Nicky Reagan,
Tommy Dunn, and Mortimer

1259
01:16:42,008 --> 01:16:44,410
Are headed for
professional football.

1260
01:16:47,613 --> 01:16:50,116
Fantastic game!

1261
01:16:50,149 --> 01:16:52,318
Oh, mate,
you played a blinder!

1262
01:16:52,351 --> 01:16:54,287
Ohh!

1263
01:17:36,362 --> 01:17:40,133
♪ We're from Tigerland

1264
01:17:40,166 --> 01:17:43,970
♪ A fighting fury
We're from Tigerland ♪

1265
01:17:44,003 --> 01:17:47,173
♪ In any weather
you will see us with a grin ♪

1266
01:17:47,206 --> 01:17:48,908
♪ Risking head and skin

1267
01:17:48,942 --> 01:17:50,910
♪ If we're behind,
we'll never mind ♪

1268
01:17:50,944 --> 01:17:52,211
♪ We'll fight and fight
and win ♪

1269
01:17:52,245 --> 01:17:54,680
♪ Oh, we're from Tigerland

1270
01:17:54,713 --> 01:17:59,252
♪ We never weaken
till the final siren sounds ♪

1271
01:17:59,285 --> 01:18:01,487
♪ Like the Tigers of old

1272
01:18:01,520 --> 01:18:02,956
♪ We're strong and we're bold

1273
01:18:02,989 --> 01:18:04,958
♪ Oh, we're from Tiger

1274
01:18:04,991 --> 01:18:06,392
♪ Yellow and black

1275
01:18:06,425 --> 01:18:09,895
♪ Oh, we're from Tigerland

1276
01:18:55,074 --> 01:18:57,310
I'm sorry.

1277
01:18:57,343 --> 01:18:58,211
Look, I appreciate it,

1278
01:18:58,244 --> 01:18:59,973
- but I don't know what...
- No, okay?

1279
01:19:00,007 --> 01:19:04,317
You guys need to find a way
to forgive and to let go.

1280
01:19:04,510 --> 01:19:06,379
I've never been
with a guy before,

1281
01:19:06,412 --> 01:19:10,383
And this footy player
who I idolized starts...

1282
01:19:10,416 --> 01:19:12,751
He's into me,
and I was too young.

1283
01:19:12,785 --> 01:19:15,321
I was too messed up
to process it.

1284
01:19:15,354 --> 01:19:19,392
I'm not the person
